CT22026059558 to the 2nd respondent submitted by the petitioner for regularisationof the extra floors constructed in the premises bearing H. No.3- 5-121lEl1l6lNo(Part) and 3-5-1211E1116, and H.No.3-5-121lEl116l tu6,Eden Bagh, Ramkote,Hyderabad. inspite of expressing my readiness to pay the penal charges, as beingillegal, arbitrary, unjust and unconstitutional and consequently direct the 2ndrespondent herein to regularise the extra floors constructed n the above mentionedpremises in terms of Se. 4554 and 455AA of the GHMC, Act-
l.A NO: 1 OF 2026
Petrtion under Section 151 CPC praying that in the circumstances stated inthe affidavit filed in support of the petition, the High Court may be pleased to directthe 2nd respondent herein to consider and dispose of the representation dated.27-l-2026 vide Acknowledge lnvoice No - CT22026059558 to the 2nd respondentpending disposal of the main Writ Petition, in the interest of justice.
Counsel for the Petitioners: SRI. SARWATH MEHDI KHAN FORMs SHAKEERA BANO,
Counsel for the Respondent No.l: GP FOR MCPL ADMN URBAN DEVCounsel for the Respondent No. 2 To 4: SRI M. ARUN KUMAR, SC FOR GHMC
