23. Learned counsel for petitioners submitted that in similar factsand circumstances, this Court disposed of Writ petition No.6241 of2026 uide order dated 27 .02.2026 with a direr:tion to respondentNo.2 therein to consider the regularization application of thepetitioners therein and to pass appropriate orders strictly inaccordance with law by duly giving fair opportunity of hearing to thepetitioner and until such time, respondent No.3 lherein was directednot to act upon the impugned notice therein. Learned counsel for thepetitioner prayed this Court to pass a similar order in the presentWrit Petition.
4. karned Standing Counsel for respondent Nos.2 to 4 did notdispute the same.
5. Accordingly, this Writ petition is disposed of in terms of orderdated 27 .02.2026 passed in Wrir petition No.624 1 of 2026, with adirection to respondent No.2 to consider the regr,rlarizationapplication of the petitioner, dated 27.O1.2026, and to passappropriate orders strictly in accordance with la\^, by duly giving fairopportunigr of hearing to petitioners and till such time, respondentNos.2 to 4 are directed not to take any coercive steps against thesubject properfy. There shall be no order as to costs.1/

