4. Perused the record
5. Earlier, the petitioners {ited W.P.No.5353 of 2026 and thepetitioners' counsel sought for withdrawal of the said writpetition granting liberty to the petitioner to seek appropriateremedy as available under law, this Court by an order dated20.02.2026 dismissed the writ petition as withdrawn grantingliberty as prayed for. Subsequently, the petitioners made arepresentation on 23.O2.2026 to respondent Nos.2 and 3 seekingregularization of the residential building constmcted at premisesbearing H.No.13-19-83, Plot No. 2i Part, Kodandaram Nagar, p& T Colony, Gaddiaannaram Division, Saroornagar, Hyderabad,under Sections 455-4 and 455-AA of the GHMC Act, 1955.
6. Heard learned Senior Counsel appearing on behalf ofpetitioners' counsel on record and learned counsel representingMr. Srinivasa Rao Pachwa, learned Stalding Counsel for GHMC,who takes notice on behalf of respondent Nos.2 ald 3.
7 . Recording the submissions of learned counsel appearingfor petitioners and respondents, without expressing any opinionon the merits of the case, the respondent No.2 is directed toconsider the petitioners' regularization application dated23.02.2026 and after giving a fair opportunit5r of hearing to the
